      "writtenOn": "2024-01-25T21:09:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The  blk_enable_sub_page_limits function is called in these 2 places:\n\n- blk_queue_max_hw_sectors()\n- blk_queue_max_segment_size()\n\nand these functions are called by the block device drivers during initialization. As part of the initialization, the drivers create their own struct queue_limits that will be set in the struct gendisk so there shouldn\u0027t be a concurrent issue here.",
      "parentUuid": "ffaa0019_b58859e6",
      "revId": "137a756ff244adc941723e3835b9bbb4c404f2d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
